<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plaisir d'amour</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Plaisir d'amour&quot; (&quot;The Pleasure of Love&quot;) is a French love song written in 1784 by the composer Jean-Paul-Égide Martini (1741–1816). Its words come from a poem by Jean-Pierre Claris de Florian (1755–1794), which appears in his novel Célestine. Martini's song was a great success.</p></div>
